 sought after so  far we merge traditional craftsmanship  and traditional fabrics with a younger  aesthetic try and engineer everything  long and slim but it's also with great  eye for stitch details and fabric so  this is the one that we're using to do  we're custom making fabrics and that's  such a cool thing could you take it to  like a 6 on the loop join is not the  easiest person to work with no no we  said this as well he has this one idea  and we just go over and over and over  all right we do the samples we do the  samples it's a very tough process but  also it's very fun well that's we'll  just stick with this yeah have you  ordered it yet  from the time I was a child I've always  been very detail-oriented I'm probably a  perfectionist when I was eight years old  I was drawing cross-trainers riding  leathers and sending them off to Nike I  think what they said was we're only  working with patent-pending designs and  we really really appreciate you  submitting your design but like he  responded and that for me was enough  I've been obsessed with fashion style  and the culture behind it for as long as  I can remember this has been the only  thing that I've really ever cared about  I'll be honest with you I'm very  dyslexic school was never really like a  area where I shined air in my business  partner was my first tutor from like  sixth grade all the way through high  school and really got me through school  like it kind of became my best friend he  always took initiative from a young age  to kind of do things that were outside  the box  he kind of coached me in how to be cool  and what to wear and we would discuss  how we would one day start this business  and I know that seems kind of crazy but  it's the truth here we are now 10 15  years looking back we've been able to do  that when we first started out Aaron and  I invested our life savings it's about  two years of living off of nothing it  was sometimes skipping meals other times  it was literally eggs and oatmeal there  were a lot of points where it would've  been very easy for us to jump off the  ship and we chose not to it was for a  bigger vision and it was a choice and we  believed in what we were creating  getting the smallest taste of freedom  working on something for yourself that  you're deeply passionate about and have  been trying to create since you were a  child there's nothing like it
 

